# The login goes away while a thread is watched, as after `gh auth logout` or an
# expired token. CST says it needs a login, reads the token again, and
# picks up once the user has logged back in. A refused login is retried every
# five minutes, so this takes about twelve.

size 110x30
arg --mux
fake_gh
session app Waiting on a reply
watch_thread https://github.com/o/r/discussions/7
timeout 330000

# Let the first poll succeed, so the account and token are already in hand.
wait 70000
expect_not Thread watching
github logged-out

wait_for Thread watching needs a login
dump 01-refused

# The next try reads the token again, and there is none.
wait_for has no token
dump 02-no-token

github up
wait_for Thread watching reached GitHub again
dump 03-logged-in-again
